<article class="env-lemma" id="09U6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09U6">Lemma <span data-tag="09U6">20.46.4</span>.</a> Let $f : (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y)$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. If $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ is a strictly perfect complex of $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-modules, then $f^*\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ is a strictly perfect complex of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The pullback of a finite free module is finite free. The functor $f^*$ is additive functor hence preserves direct summands. The lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>